loguru
------------------------------------------
Lightweight and flexible C++ logging library

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libloguru-devel-2.2.0-1bl1
  libloguru2-2.2.0-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/emilk/loguru

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/emilk/loguru/archive/refs/tags/v2.2.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack loguru-2.2.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./loguru-2.2.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/loguru-2.2.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/loguru-2.2.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libloguru2-2.2.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libloguru-devel-2.2.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(loguru)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/loguru.README
  /usr/share/doc/loguru/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/loguru/README.md

(libloguru2)
  /usr/bin/cygloguru-2.dll

(libloguru-devel)
  /usr/include/loguru/loguru.hpp
  /usr/lib/cmake/loguru/loguru-config-version.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/loguru/loguru-config.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/loguru/loguru-targets-relwithdebinfo.cmake
  /usr/lib/cmake/loguru/loguru-targets.cmake
  /usr/lib/libloguru.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/loguru.pc

